\cf0 \'91*_Spikes.mat\'92 contains combined neurons from all sessions. For each neuron, the timestamps (in \uc0\u956 s), session ID, channel ID, cluster ID, and recording brain area are stored in the variables \'91timestampsOfCellAll\'92, \'91vCell\'92, \'91vCh\'92, \'91vClusterID\'92, and \'91areaCell\'92, respectively (note that these variables were all matched). There are three variables that describe spike sorting quality. The variable \'91IsoDist\'92 shows the isolation distance value for each cluster (i.e., a single\
neuron). The variable \'91statsSNR\'92 contains 6 columns: 1\'97session ID, 2\'97channel ID, 3\'97cluster ID, 4\'97the average signal-to-noise ratio (SNR), 5\'97inter-spike intervals (ISI) that are below 3 ms, and 6\'97peak SNR. The variable \'91statsProjectAll\'92 contains 5 columns: 1\'97session ID, 2\'97 channel ID, 3 and 4\'97IDs for a cluster pair, and 5\'97pairwise distance between two clusters.\
\
Usage note: Please refer to \'91Anlysis/Code/CategoryNeuronSelection.m\'92 for a demonstration of identifying identity neurons. Please see \'91Anlysis/Code/plotRastersSampleIdentityCell.m\'92 for a demonstration of plotting spike train and temporal response of example neurons. Please  see \'92Anlysis/Code/PlotSortingQuality.m\'92  for the plotting of the sorting qulaity. \
